\s1 The Covenant at Horeb
\p \v 1 \w Then Moses|strong="H04872"\w* \w summoned|strong="H07121"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w and said|strong="H00559"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00413"\w* \w to them|strong="H00413"\w*:\f + \fr 5:1 \ft Note that Deuteronomy 5:1 through Deuteronomy 26:19 may be presented as a continuous section of unbroken speech by Moses. In place of multiple levels of nested quotes, this section has been set apart with a double space.\f*
\p \w Hear|strong="H08085"\w*, \w O Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the statutes|strong="H02706"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and ordinances|strong="H04941"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I|strong="H00595"\w* \w declare|strong="H01696"\w* \w in your hearing|strong="H00241"\w* \w this day|strong="H03117"\w*. \w Learn|strong="H03925"\w* \w them|strong="H00853"\w* \w and observe them|strong="H06213"\w* \w carefully|strong="H08104"\w*. \v 2 \w The LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w our God|strong="H00430"\w* \w made|strong="H03772"\w* \w a covenant|strong="H01285"\w* \w with us|strong="H05973"\w* \w at Horeb|strong="H02722"\w*.\f + \fr 5:2 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f*
