\p \v 16 \w Three|strong="H07969"\w* \w times|strong="H06471"\w* \w a year|strong="H08141"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w your men|strong="H02138"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00854"\w* \w are to appear|strong="H07200"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w your God|strong="H00430"\w* \w in the place|strong="H04725"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w He will choose|strong="H00977"\w*: \w at the Feast|strong="H02282"\w* \w of Unleavened Bread|strong="H04682"\w*,\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, the seven-day period after the Passover during which no leaven may be eaten; see Exodus 12:14–20.\f* \w the Feast|strong="H02282"\w* \w of Weeks|strong="H07620"\w*,\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as \fqa the Feast of Harvest\ft (see Exodus 23:16) or \fqa the Feast of Pentecost\ft (see Acts 2:1).\f* \w and the Feast|strong="H02282"\w* \w of Tabernacles|strong="H05521"\w*.\f + \fr 16:16 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see Exodus 23:16 and Exodus 34:22).\f* \w No one|strong="H03808"\w* \w should appear|strong="H07200"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00854"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w empty-handed|strong="H07387"\w*. \v 17 \w Everyone|strong="H00376"\w* \w must appear with a gift|strong="H04979"\w* \w as he is able|strong="H03027"\w*, \w according to the blessing|strong="H01293"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w your God|strong="H00430"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w has given|strong="H05414"\w* you.
\s1 Judges and Justice
